# In a ness project, session-start for a conversation that is not a ness session prints the
# unbound note and touches no row; outside a ness project, and for pre-tool, it stays silent.
# covers: R-HOOK-019, R-HOOK-002
exec git init -q -b main plain
cd plain
stdin ../startup.json
exec ness hook session-start
! stdout .
! stderr .
cd ../repo
exec ness init --gate true --base main --yes
exec git add -A
exec git commit -q -m 'ness init'
stdin ../startup.json
exec ness hook session-start
cmp stdout ../note.txt
! stderr .
env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=0bad0bad-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
stdin ../startup.json
exec ness hook session-start
cmp stdout ../note.txt
stdin ../pretool.json
exec ness hook pre-tool
! stdout .
! stderr .
exec ness status --json
! stdout '"id"'

-- startup.json --
{"hook_event_name":"SessionStart","source":"startup","session_id":"0bad0bad-0000-4000-8000-000000000001"}
-- pretool.json --
{"hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"sleep 30; ness inbox"}}
-- note.txt --
ness: this conversation is not a ness session yet.
Answer questions here directly. Work that needs a branch (a quick task or a full session) runs
as a session: load the ness-entry skill and promote this conversation with
ness open --root --here --scope NAME --tier TIER --size quick|full --brief FILE
quick: one deliverable, no children, one sitting; full: anything else. You can change it later
with ness size. Propose it in one line first, unless the operator already asked you to start the work.
